<article class="env-lemma" id="08AH">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/08AH">Lemma <span data-tag="08AH">66.24.4</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $X$ be a Noetherian algebraic space over $S$. Let $\overline{x}$ be a geometric point of $X$. Then $\mathcal{O}_{X, \overline{x}}$ is a Noetherian local ring. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Choose an étale neighbourhood $(U, \overline{u})$ of $\overline{x}$ where $U$ is a scheme. Then $\mathcal{O}_{X, \overline{x}}$ is the strict henselization of the local ring of $U$ at $u$, see Lemma <a href="/tag/04KF" data-tag="04KF">66.22.1</a>. By our definition of Noetherian spaces the scheme $U$ is locally Noetherian. Hence we conclude by More on Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/06LJ" data-tag="06LJ">15.46.3</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>